#passage(("You have 12 Imams: alBaqir, asSadiq, 'Ali, alHussayn, alHassan, all of these people. What are the characteristics of these 12 Imams? Shi'a belief is to believe there's 12 Imams appointed. There has to always be an appointed Imam at every time, divinely appointed by God. And these Imams have the knowledge of the unseen. They're infallible. They do not commit any errors or mistakes at all, zero. In many books, it mentions that they're better than all the Prophets, except Prophet Muhammad. So these are the 12 Imams. That's the first thing.", "Second thing is, what is the Shi'a view on the Sahaba الصحابة (the Companions of the Prophetﷺ)? They will say that the overwhelming majority, except nine, or three, the overwhelming majority, which is over 100,000 in the last sermon of the Prophet, they're not believers. And they're evil people. And the wife of the Prophetﷺ also: they would curse the wives and say the wives are not believers.", "The third belief, a very important belief: they would say that there are verses of the Quran that are to be read or understood in a different way. Many, many verses, even in وضوء (Wudu: Ablution). There's many verses and many narrations about that. The fourth thing is that they would bring narrations; of course this is all just attributions, but the overwhelming majority, over 90%, are coming from alBaqir asSadiq. So these are the main beliefs of Shi'a, the twelvers, the Ja'faris, which is the overwhelming majority of the Shi'a.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Fully Dismantles The Shia Position! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t7vhKiTrvNA", ((202, "3:22–5:44"), (346, "5:46–6:54"), (423, "7:03–7:52"),))
