#passage(("There's multiple sects within Shiism itself, so let me just talk about the most common, which is the Twelver Shias or Jaafaries or Ithna’asharies. They have different names.", "They believe that the Companions of the Prophet, except three or nine, all of the rest of them are disbelievers; they're Hypocrites, they were acting to be Believers and they left Islam. And then they believe that there are 12 people called Imams that we need to follow, better than the prophets of God, except Prophet Muhammedﷺ according to some of them; some of them, they say even better than Prophet Muhammedﷺ. So they make it a race thing: we're only going to follow the lineage of prophet Muhammedﷺ, which comes through his cousin Ali and his daughter Fatima. Their lineage comes from Al-Hassan and Al-Hussain. Those 12 Imams will come from that lineage. And all of the Companions of the Prophetﷺ, who’s transmitted everything to us, are a bunch of hypocrites and disbelievers. And also they accuse the wives of the Prophet Muhammedﷺ of the same, and they say that they committed adultery.", "So what we say to them is this: the Quran praises the Companions, commands us to follow the Companions, and Allah says he prepared Paradise for them. In the (Quran9:100) Allah is saying these are good people that are going to go to Paradise; you should follow them. And we have a Shia telling us they're bad people. Which one do we follow? Do we follow the Quran or do we follow that one person? The Quran itself commands you: when you disagree, you go back to the Quran. So if we apply the criteria, we see the Quran tells us the Companions are good people, so we follow them. We see the Quran doesn't speak about anything to do with the 12 imams. It only says to follow the Prophet and the Companions.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Skeptical About The Prophet of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QIxWrKc_J_Y", ((2209, "36:49–37:00"), (2226, "37:06–37:59"), (2283, "38:03–38:33"),))
