#passage(("They talked about the Imams knowing the unseen. Allah explicitly in the Quran says the only one who knows the unseen is Him. Allahﷻ says in the Quran: (Annaml27:65) قُل لَّا يَعْلَمُ مَن فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ الْغَيْبَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ (Say no one in the heavens and the earth knows the unseen except Allah.)", "Allahﷻ says: (Aljinn72:26) عَالِمُ الْغَيْبِ (The knower of the unseen.) Now let's see the only exception, who Allah tells the unseen to. It's there in this verse. Allah says: عَالِمُ الْغَيْبِ فَلَا يُظْهِرُ عَلَىٰ غَيْبِهِ أَحَدًا (The knower of the unseen, he does not reveal the unseen to anyone). (alJinn72:27) إِلَّا مَنِ ارْتَضَىٰ مِن رَّسُولٍ (Except who he pleases from a Messenger). So who can He give the unseen to? Only a Messenger. The Imams are not Messengers with the agreement.", "Now they say that they are higher. You can't even find them in the Quran. Why are you talking about them being higher? Give me evidence. Where does Allah say they are higher or better? You've not proved that Imam is a status higher than a Prophet. You have a lot of false assumptions, and then you make a conclusion based on them. We believe that Prophets were all Imams. Imams mean they led their people. So Allah referring to them as an Imam there, meaning a leader of their people, it is a linguistic usage; we don't have an issue that someone leads their people. They were all leading the people. And Allah mentioned their praise, that they were the best of the people, and then Allah says those are the ones that Allah guided, so follow their guidance: أُولَٰئِكَ الَّذِينَ هَدَى اللَّهُ ۖ فَبِهُدَاهُمُ اقْتَدِهْ (alAna'am6:90) (These are the ones who Allah guided. So follow their guidance.)", "Allah says: (Albaqara2:253) تِلْكَ الرُّسُلُ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ These Messengers, We elevated one over the others in degrees. So Allah talks about their praise and them having these highest degrees. Where is anything to do with Imams? Not even mentioned, let alone to talk about their praise! It's not there. First you need to prove your premise. Where is the proof for your premise? And then we talk about whether it's a higher status and where are the verses and the understanding.", "Also, the idea of infallibility: there is nothing in the Quran that would talk about that. This is something explicit about the Prophetﷺ. For example, Allahﷻ says: (Oh Prophet, deliver what Allah has given to you.) (And if you don't, you've not delivered His Message) In chapter (alMaida5:67). And then Allah says وَاللَّهُ يَعْصِمُكَ مِنَ النَّاسِ: gives you 'Issma, gives you infallibility in delivery of the Message. So whatever you deliver about the Message will be correct.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Fully Dismantles The Shia Position! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t7vhKiTrvNA", ((2127, "35:27–35:38"), (2148, "35:48–36:08"), (2193, "36:33–37:27"), (2250, "37:30–37:52"), (2291, "38:11–38:30"),))
