#passage(("As People of the Sunnah, we don't believe the Sahaba were infallible. We don't need their names mentioned in the Quran. Whether it's mentioned in the Quran or it's not mentioned in the Quran, it doesn't matter, because for us, we're not believing that they're divinely appointed people that exist in every time, that are infallible, that know the unseen, that they are the only people who know the interpretation of the Quran. That's your religion! It doesn't matter for us if the names of the Sahaba are not mentioned, because we don't believe they’re Imams; you do! Our creed is not built upon the names of the Sahaba.", "I didn't ask you for the names of the Imams; I asked you for the concept of Imama. Where is it in the Quran? Where does Allah say there are 12 Imams that are infallible, that you need to follow, that they have the understanding of the Quran? It does NOT exist in the Quran. The concept doesn't exist. Then on top of it, the names don't exist, while the names of the infallible people exist: مُّحَمَّدٌۭ رَّسُولُ ٱللَّهِ ۚ (Muhammad the Messenger of God) (alFath48:29); وَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٞ قَدۡ خَلَتۡ مِن قَبۡلِهِ ٱلرُّسُلُۚ (Muhammad is not but a Messenger...) (al'Emran3:144). The Prophetﷺ, his name is mentioned in the Quran. Musa (Moses) is mentioned in the Quran, 'Isa (Jesus) is mentioned in the Quran, Nuh (Noah) is mentioned in the Quran, Adam is mentioned. All of the infallible Prophets are named in the Quran.", "You believe the Imams are better than the Prophets, and some say: except Prophet Muhammad. If the Imams are better than the Prophets, then how can the Quran mention the names of people who are lesser, and not mention the names of people who are more important?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Shia Girl Confronts Muslim On His Claims Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LcbjBQElXe0", ((1095, "18:15–18:50"), (1139, "18:59–19:33"), (1182, "19:42–19:55"),))
