#passage(("Does Allah in the Quran talk about the prayer? The Quran does mention different times of the prayer: أَقِمِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ لِدُلُوكِ ٱلشَّمۡسِ إِلَىٰ غَسَقِ ٱلَّیۡلِ وَقُرۡءَانَ ٱلۡفَجۡرِۖ (alIsraa17:78). This is one verse, and there's another verse in Surat Taha (20) which mentions all of the times.", "So you brought the example of the prayer. So here's my response. The Quran mentions the prayer. The Quran mentions the times of the prayer. The Quran mentioned things that we do in the prayer. And the Quran tells us that the prayer is something that we're commanded to do, and that if we do not do, then it can lead us to Hellfire. Now, all of this is information about the prayer in the Quran. Now find me information about the Imams in the Quran, anything: 1- that we're told to follow the 12 Imams; 2- that they are a part of our religion; 3- that it's a sin not to believe in them, like what we have about the prayer; 4- or that they are 12 to begin with, or that there is Imams.", "I'm going to make this argument: anything which is a foundational thing of Islam, like the prayer, is going to be found in the Quran, and many aspects of it is going to be found in the Quran. I'm not asking you to find me every single thing. But where is the concept in the Quran? There are hundreds of verses in the Quran that talk about the prayer. Hundreds. Now bring me one verse. I'm not going to ask you for 10, 5; I'm not going to even ask you for 3. Bring me one verse in the Quran that, in any way, shape, or form, talks to you about the 12 Imams and the need to follow these 12 Imams.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Shia Girl Confronts Muslim On His Claims Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LcbjBQElXe0", ((227, "3:47–4:54"), (332, "5:32–6:04"), (370, "6:10–6:53"),))
