// U ML092:409-575 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("Allah says to Ibrahimﷺ إِنِّى جَاعِلُكَ لِلنَّاسِ إِمَامًۭا ۖ (alBaqara2:124). Allah says to Ibrahim (I'm going to make you an Imam). And then, Ibrahimﷺ says: وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِى (and from my lineage?). And then Allah says: لَا يَنَالُ عَهْدِى ٱلظَّـٰلِمِينَ (the Dhalimeen [wrong doers] don't get my covenant). What does that have to do with your 12 Imams?", "This is the problem with the Shi'a: you quote a verse from the Quran about Ibrahimﷺ that has nothing to do with the Imams, and then you go to a hadith that has nothing to do with the verse. You said that Ibrahimﷺ asked Allah to make him an Imam. Now: was Musaﷺ (Moses) an Imam? That's one of the 5 main Prophets of Islam. That's from أُولُو العَزمِ مِنَ الرُّسُل (alAhqaf46:35). When Allah says in the Quran: (alBaqara2:253) تِلْكَ ٱلرُّسُلُ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍۢ ۘ (These Messengers we raised in grace over one another), Allah mentions: مِّنْهُم مَّن كَلَّمَ ٱللَّهُ ۖ (from them who spoke to Allah), referring to Musaﷺ, for his high status.", "What does the word Imam mean? The Prophetﷺ told us the meaning of the word: إِنَّمَا جُعِلَ الإِمَامُ لِيُؤْتَمَّ بِهِ (The Imam is the person that you do Imama of, that you follow). So if you're a leader of your people, a righteous leader, and you lead the people, and people take you as an example and follow you, that's what an Imam is. So Musaﷺ was an Imam of his people.", "But you said that Allah says in the verse: لَا يَنَالُ عَهْدِي الظَّالِمِينَ (That anyone who does Dhulm [injustice] to himself, cannot be an Imam). So Musaﷺ did Dhulm to himself. So how can he be an Imam? Musaﷺ explicitly says in the Quran: رَبِّ إِنِّي ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِي (I have did Dhulm to myself) (alQasas28:16). How is Musaﷺ an Imam, like you claim, and in the same time, he did Dhulm to himself? And you said anyone who does Dhulm to himself cannot be an Imam! Yunusﷺ (Jonas) in the belly of the whale, he said: (alAnbiya21:87) لَّآ إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنتَ سُبْحَـٰنَكَ إِنِّى كُنتُ مِن