#passage(("I know this Quran, alhamdulillah, from beginning to end. There's no name of Ali in the Quran from beginning to end, just like there's no name of [Abu Bakr]. The verse you brought has nothing to do with what you're saying. I'll tell you why.", "What you're referring to is translation. Translation is a word for word changing the word from Arabic into English. I'm not adding anything there; I'm just translating the words. I'm an Arab; this is my language. It says the Believers that give the [zakat] and establish the prayer, and it says: and they're kneeling down or prostrating. Where's Ali there?", "We stick to the Quran. Why do we stick to the Quran? Because I know that if you don't stick to the Quran, you go somewhere else; you keep bringing different things; we'll go everywhere. But when you stick to the Quran, you have no Foundation. The verse here has nothing about [Ali]. Now your interpretation from your books is irrelevant, because I can bring an interpretation from another book, and then you're not going to accept it.", "Let's accept this interpretation, this understanding; let's take it, there's no problem. If I now give [zakat] when I'm [prostrating], does this verse include me? Do I become the leader of the Muslims? The verse here says \"those who believe\". It's referring to all the Believers. So I'm a Believer, [alhamdulillah]; I believe in Allah and his messenger. If I prostrate now and I give [Zakat], does that mean I become now the leader? What makes a person now the leader based on this verse, and if I do the same thing, and I'm a Believer, and the [verse] includes me, I'm not a leader? What's the difference? This verse doesn't help you, because it's a general verse, and it can be applied to all the Believers, because it doesn't specify one person.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Afghan Shia Questions Muslim On Sunnism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pszdC9gMHIk", ((1175, "19:35–19:56"), (1228, "20:28–22:18"), (1376, "22:56–23:16