#passage(("There are clear authentic reports in al-kafi in which the imam is being asked if he's an imam, and he's outright denying it. Of course, according to your criteria it's [mutawatir], because we have more than one hadith that does say this. The question is: how are sunnis [blameworthy] for rejecting the imams and the [Imamah] of the imams?", "The reason why it's not the same is because in [tashayyu'] this is a part of the deen. You have the imams saying that rejecting one imam is rejecting all the imams; those that do not know the imam of their times, he dies the death of [jahiliyyah], and this is the death of [kufr] and [nifaq]. The problem with this is that I'm asking: how is this binding? How are we blameworthy? And by the way, these reports of [Sunnis] going to hellfire for rejecting the imam: this is [mutawatir] according to your standards, because, as you said, two narrators are enough. And it's [blameworthy] for not knowing the imams, even though the imams, according to tawatur, they rejected being imams. This is according to you, according to your standards.",), "Farid Responds, “Full Debate: Farid (Sunni) vs Bayat (Shia)”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Iwc31dHLfco", ((680, "11:20–11:45"), (1093, "18:13–19:39"),))
