#passage(("The reason why 160 million Shia believe in this idea of a hidden, infallible [Imam], divinely appointed, that was born and then went into occultation (which is a fancy way of saying hidden and inaccessible) for 1,200 years: there's this crazy backstory to it. We take it for granted, and the average modern [Shia] today accepts it wholeheartedly, has absolute faith in it, but back then it was a matter of extreme confusion. You had a lot of people just leaving Shiism because this idea just seemed so strange.", "In any case, it's a mixture of two things really: one has to do with a war between these tax collectors, and another one is a personal inheritance issue. All the information I'm providing you, it's not my personal research; this is all based on a [Shia] scholar named [Hossein Modarressi]. He's a professor at the University of Princeton. He's written this really good book called Crisis and Consolidation, and he [spends] a good chunk of it just explaining the situation and what led to this situation that caused all these people to accept the existence of someone who doesn't exist. Now, it sounds conspiratorial, but the conspiracy is what they believe, to be honest.",), "Farid Responds, “Why Shias believe the Mahdi is 1200 years old”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bT7GyUntorM", ((0, "0:00–0:39"), (39, "0:39–1:37"),))
