#passage(("Ahlus-Sunnah ARE PEOPLE OF EVIDENCE. If you don't have proof for something, you shouldn't believe it.", "Allah says in the Quran, Chapter:9 of the Quran, verse:100: So the first group of people, from the Muhajirun and Ansar. Muhajirun, we already know who Muhajirun are: people who migrated, did hijrah from Mecca to Medina, with the Prophetﷺ, which were all Sahaba. Ansar are all the Sahaba: Aws & Khazraj, which are the 2 tribes that were in Medina, that protected the Prophet, and did Nusra of him: supported him. So those are all the Sahaba, which include, by the way, Abu Bakr and 'Umar and 'Uthman and all of these people.", "Allah says, those Muhajirun and Ansar, And then Allah says: وَٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوهُم بِإِحْسَـٰنٍۢ. What does اتّبَع mean? FOLLOW! Where does it say to FOLLOW the Sahaba? An explicit verse. It cannot get more shiny than this. And the verse doesn't only say follow them. The verse is: those who follow them, it says, Allah is pleased with them And they are pleased with Him. Is that it? No! And Allah prepared, for those people who follow the Sahaba, Jannat (gardens) which rivers flow beneath, And that is the Great Success. So not just a verse that just says follow the Sahaba, but it says the outcome of following the Sahaba is the pleasure of Allah upon you, and paradise, which is the goal of every Muslim.", "Now, is that the only verse? There is many many verses which talk about the virtues of the Sahaba. It talks about how those Sahaba are believers (alAnfal8:74), How Allah is pleased with them, How they have paradise (atTawba9:100), All of them, by the way. Like Surat alHadeed: It talks about (alHadeed57:10) (It's not equal, those who spent and fought before the conquest of Mecca, and those who did after). And then Allah says that those who did before are greater in degree, Because of course, it was more difficult. Before the conquest of Mecca, things were difficult, So those who fought and spent money, they have more rewards than those who did after, and things were easier. But then Allah says: وَكُلًّۭا وَعَدَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ. The حُسْنَىٰ, from فُعْلَىٰ in the Arabic language, which means the greatest reward. What is the greatest reward? It's Jannah, of course, it's paradise. Allah is saying in the Quran (alHadeed57:10), those Companions, all of them, That fought and spent before the conquest, and those who did after, which includes all of those companions, Allahﷻ has promised them Husna.", "Allah says in the Quran (alFath48:29): (Prophet Muhammadﷺ is the Messenger of Allah) (Those who are with him). Who is with him? It's no one except the Sahaba. (They're strong against the disbelievers) (They are merciful with each other). You see them \"Ruku' & Sujood\" (bowing & prostrating), the famous verse of Ruku' & Sujood, And give the Zakat and Sadaqah (obligatory and voluntary charity). Here Allah describes the Sahaba: (You see them prostrating, seeking a bounty from Allahﷻ). And then Allah says (alFAth48:29): Their example in the Torah is like this, and their example in the Injil. So Allah have parables, examples of the Sahaba in the Torah and the Injil, of their good virtues. Not only does the Quran record all of these good virtues, Allahﷻ talks about the Companions in Bay'ah: Pledge of allegiance (alFath48:18). Allah calls the Mu'mineen (Believers) first, And then Allah says that He is pleased with them. He knew what was in their heart. Allah knew that they had a pure heart; Allah knew they came to do Bay'ah to protect the Prophetﷺ, to protect this religion.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Shia Follower Gets An Unexpected Reality Check! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6v8T06xoukk", ((666, "11:06–11:24"), (702, "11:42–12:19"), (766, "12:46–13:30"), (816, "13:36–14:45"), (888, "14:48–15:58"),))
