#passage(("You got people in the [Shia] tradition that, even though they don't accept Muslim or [Bukhari], will use [a hadith] there, and they will mis-explain [the hadith], which is a wrong explanation of it. They don't accept these books to be authentic, but they use [a hadith] there for some reason, and then they say: look, this Hadith means this. This is in the day of judgment, where the Prophet will be on the [Hawd]: if you drink, you're never going to be thirsty again. Then the prophet will say: my companions, come. And then the angels will say: no, they're not going to come, because you do not know what they did after you.", "So then how do [scholars] explain that? There was a group of people, many people who apostate after the prophet. There was something called [Ridda] Wars, which happen against [apostates]. When the prophet died it was a shock for many people. There was many Hypocrites among the Muslims; when he died, it was the opportunity for them. So this is referring to those people who left Islam after the death of the Prophet. But who actually spread Islam to Iraq, or spread Islam to Afghanistan, or spread Islam to Iran were the companions. Without those people I wouldn't know Islam; they wouldn't be Muslims on Earth today. If those people were not truly people who held Islam to be of high regard and truly believed in this religion, they would not have spread it from Morocco to China.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Afghan Shia Questions Muslim On Sunnism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pszdC9gMHIk", ((400, "6:40–7:20"), (441, "7:21–8:08"),))
