#passage(("The reality is I cannot accuse everyone of it. There are people who are honest about the reality; They don't believe in these things. But if we go to the scholarly level, government level, I think it's a different story. You don't get to be the president of a country where your beliefs are different than the beliefs of his scholars. That wouldn't make any sense to me. It wouldn't be something that makes common sense, that you would allow those people to be on the [minbar]. So how are you allowing them, when you're the president, to do this, if it's such a bad thing? Nobody knows anyone's heart, but what we know is what's written in the books. If someone says I don't believe this, I'll take their word for it. I'm not going to say this guy's pretending. This guy is not pretending. Okay, you don't believe it; I appreciate it. That's how it should be. Allah says the wives of the prophet are our mothers. Can you curse your own mother? Can you say your mother was this? Your mother was that?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sneako Questions The Muslim Lantern On Shia & Sunni Unity | The Iran War And More | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kdFNc6Jr6OQ", ((1647, "27:27–28:28"),))

