#passage(("He's trying to focus on the reliability of one narrator, [Ibn Jumay'], who [Ibn Hazm] clearly has a problem with. But let's [concede] there's no issue with him. Do you know how many people are between [Ibn Hazm] and...? Just to give you an idea, there's six people between [Ibn Hazm and Imam] Muslim, and then an additional three people to get [to Ibn Jumay'], who by the way isn't even a sahabi, and he only [narrates] from the youngest of the companions. Who are these people? We got no idea, and [Ibn Hazm] didn't tell us, so there's no way of knowing who the narrators are, and there's no way of authenticating this report and accepting the ascription to [Ibn Jumay']. And of course there's the other issue of: we don't know who is getting this specific report from. Why does he think that this is an authentic report that he can use? I don't know.", "Nothing in this report says that Omar is asking if he himself is one of the Raiders that tried to kill the prophet, peace be upon him. The report merely has Omar asking [Hudhayfa]: did the prophet, peace be upon Him, name me? Meaning, as a hypocrite. Amar, you got to be very careful in the words that you ascribe to a report. Now secondly, the source that you are quoting is in the 8th Century after [Hijrah], so there is [no isnad]. Shia look up to you, and you have to raise their level by providing at least reports that have chains, not reports with no chains like the previous report. Imagine I was quoting some 10, 11th century [Shia] source with no isnad.", "However, I'm going to read to you the Hadith that [Ammar] was quoting, from a second century Source, six centuries before the source that [Ammar] was quoting from. This is saying: passed by me while I was in the Masjid. He said: Oh [Hudhayfa], so and so had died, so go attend, meaning attend his funeral prayer. He then left to leave the Masid, and he turned to me and saw me just sitting there, so he realized and came to me (meaning he realized that [Hudhayfa] didn't pray because the man is a hypocrite). He said: Oh [Hudhayfa], I ask you by Allah, am I one of them? Meaning, am I one of the Hypocrites? He said: by Allah, no, and I will not [acquit] anyone after you. I then saw Omar's eyes filled with tears.", "Consider something: this report, which you're not going to accept, but this report is written as a merit for Omar. You can assume it's a fabrication, but you have to admit it's written as a merit for Omar, most likely after the death of Omar. It's narrated as a merit: you come off reading this report feeling like Omar was a good person, even if you don't believe the report. Of course, if you reject the report, then forget about it, but it's written as a merit. What boggles my mind is someone like [Ammar] would read this report and would think: this is a clear confession by Omar that he tried to kill the prophet. So those of you who approached reports and read them in such a way, the only thing I got to say to you is: you got to fix your heart.",), "Farid Responds, “Ammar Nakshawani / Assassination of the Prophet ﷺ [Debunked]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jrjb6KE0FJ4", ((161, "2:41–3:53"), (335, "5:35–6:38"), (398, "6:38–8:00"), (483, "8:03–9:00"),))

