#passage(("Muslims don't have an issue with Ahl alBayt; we love and respect them. They are the household of the Prophetﷺ. Of course, we honor them, we respect them, we love them, and we follow them. But what they attribute to them is all false. Who are you supposed to follow? If you're supposed to follow the Companions, and those who follow the Companions in righteousness, Then we have those who follow the Companions in righteousness: Imam Ahmad, alBukhari, Muslim, atTirmidhi. Those are the people who took from the Companions and followed them in righteousness. Those who brought us the Quran were the Companions of the Prophetﷺ. Will a group of disbelievers die to spread the Message of Islam all the way from China to Spain? The only reason those people who refer to themselves as Shi'a, or as Muslim, is because the Sahaba did this. They would not have even known about Islam. And they will say, they're not believers!", "We mentioned the verse of the Quran (anNisa4: 59): If you disagree over anything, you return it to Allah, meaning the Quran, and then the Messenger. Now the second part, you return it to the Messenger: you will see they don't return anything to the Messenger, because what they have, all of the narrations, 90 or 95% is going to alBaqir, alSadiq, Not the Prophetﷺ.", "So they take from the Sunni Hadiths. Ghadir Khum is one of the most narrated Hadiths out there. We don't have a problem with it; We accept it. But the question is the word Waliy (Ally): It has many meanings in the Arabic language. And we take a meaning based on a context, based on the fact that we follow the Companions who told us what the context was, because they were there. And Allah told us to follow them. So which one: we take the context of the people who were there, who Allah told us they are good people, the best people who will have paradise, or we take your context, of someone who was never there, never attended, has no idea, And they're telling us: no, no, actually, the word means this, and they were all evil people? Which one should we take?", "And we all believe that Waliy is Ally. If you are Ally, you're a friend; or to love 'Ali is a part of belief and faith, because he was from the Companions, and he was praised, and he was promised Jannah, and he was one of the bravest people to fight. But religion is not about an individual. It's about the Quran that comes from Allah. It's not about Abu Bakr; It's not about 'Umar. Do you know the least of narrations that we have are from Abu Bakr and 'Umar anyways? The least number of narrations of Hadith that we have. Majority of the Hadith that we have are from Abu Hurayra, Abdullah ibn 'Umar, etc.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Fully Dismantles The Shia Position! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t7vhKiTrvNA", ((2358, "39:18–40:10"), (2424, "40:24–40:38"), (2445, "40:45–41:26"), (2492, "41:32–42:05"),))
