#passage(("First of all, who is this man? Someone that converted to Islam early on, when the Muslims were a minority. He feared for his life, because he was going to get killed. He's forced to leave his home. Of course the [Muhajirun], all of them, they're in a state of weakness, and they cannot face the oppression of the kufar; some of them are actually killed. So he leaves his home along with them. When they're in Medina, they're fighting their own original tribe. They're all fighting side by side with the prophet peace be upon them in order to allow Islam to survive. Everything that he's doing, he's doing [in] adherence to the prophet peace be upon him, because he believes in The Message of Islam and he believes in the Prophet peace be upon him.", "So now, with this in mind, when Omar says the prophet peace be upon Him is overcome with pain, is it likelier that Omar is saying this because he wants to prevent the prophet peace be upon him from delivering his message, and from preventing his will? Or is it likelier that Omar actually sincerely sees the prophet peace be upon him being overcome with pain, and he wants whatever the prophet peace be upon Him is going to dictate to do it later, when he's better?", "Now keep in mind, the prophet peace be upon Him is unable to pray in the [masjid] despite it being a few meters away, because of the pain he's in. The prophet peace be upon Him is passing out every once in a while. The prophet peace be upon Him is suffering twice as much as the average person. So why not just wait for him to get better? And I know people are thinking: but he's on his deathbed, he's not going to get better. Well, Omar didn't know that. When the prophet peace be upon Him died, [Omar] denied it. He couldn't believe it, even thought that the prophet peace be upon him was getting better, and he didn't know that the prophet peace be upon him was on his actual deathbed.", "Think of it this way: you have a [sheikh] who you adore, who you appreciate, and he's really sick. You're going to go to him and say \"teach us Hadith\", or are you going to wait a few days until he gets better? If you were in that position, what would you do?", "Remember, the prophet peace be upon Him kicks everyone out of the house, even the people that want him to dictate whatever he was going to say. Are you saying that Ali wasn't there at the time? The prophet peace be upon Him kicks out everyone.", "It doesn't say that Omar said that the prophet peace be upon Him is delirious. It says: they said, is he delirious? Is he delirious, question mark. First of all, and again, this could be said about anyone. Anyone that you hate, you can say this about. If you're a [Nasibi], you can say: [Ali] definitely didn't want the prophet to write his will. Or something more believable: his will was going to be about Abu Bakr. He wanted [Abu] Bakr to become the next [Caliph]. He just appointed [Abu] Bakr to lead the prayer, and now he wants to include [Abu] Bakr as the next [Caliph]. Someone can say this. Now, I'm not going to say this, because there's no evidence for this, in the same way there's no evidence that the prophet peace be upon Him wanted to appoint [Ali]. So we're not people of whims, we're not people of desires, we're people of [daleel], and we only speak with [daleel].",), "Farid Responds, “Ammar Nakshawani Accuses Umar (ra) of Denying the Will of the Prophet ﷺ”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GBO5TafF4LE", ((212, "3:32–4:30"), (270, "4:30–5:04"), (304, "5:04–5:47"), (347, "5:47–6:06"), (390, "6:30–6:46"), (479, "7:59–8:54"),))
