#passage(("The Shia, they need no introduction. Most of us know about the Shia; alhamdulillah, we know the problems that they have. But the Shia, they have different groups. Some of the groups of the Shia are the [Zaydis], for example. They were closest among the [Shia] [to Ahl al-Sunnah]. Then you have the majority of them. We use many names for them, but they are the majority: they are the [Twelvers], the ones that believe in 12 imams. [They're] the overwhelming majority today.", "What is our issue with them? First, they call themselves [Shia]. What does [Shia] mean? It means group. But if you add a name, then the party [of], or the group of [Ali], the cousin of the Prophet, may Allah be pleased with him. We love him and we [revere] him. But do you see the same thing I told you before: these groups go back always to one individual. They always attributed themselves to an individual. You see this always happening. In most cases, you see that they're always attributing themselves, bringing the beliefs from somewhere, and these beliefs have to come from an individual, because they're not sourced in the Quran and Sunnah. If they were sourced in the Quran, they wouldn't need to call themselves after the name of someone.", "So what do they do? Of course, they exaggerate. We said we praise him, we love him, but they go to the extent of: some of them, they call upon him for help in need, whenever they're in a problem, instead of calling upon Allah. Some of them say he was born in the [Kaaba]; many of them say he was born inside the [Kaaba]. Some of them say [Jibril] was coming, but he made a mistake: instead of going to the prophet, he went to [Ali]. None of this is made up. This is literally in their books. So we're not saying all of them believe this, because you come across: \"I don't believe this\". Say: okay, yes, but open your books and read them; see what your teachers or your scholars said. This is what they say. And they curse the Companions and the wives of the prophet sallallahu alaihi.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((8346, "2:19:06–2:19:48"), (8391, "2:19:51–2:20:52"), (8452, "2:20:52–2:21:50"),))
