#passage(("Shia didn't exist at the time of the prophet عليه الصلاة والسلام. But Sunni Muslims has always existed, which is to follow the Prophet, follow the Sunnah of the Prophet. So this is a new thing that people made up. There's a political disagreement: some issue happened, a person was killed. Some people wanted to avenge the blood of that person, and then there was Ali; he said it's not the time right now, there will be riots if we avenge his blood. So then these two groups disagreed with one another, and the group that aligned with Ali, they said we're Shia. They called themselves Shia, and then later on, they started a new religion. They brought beliefs. Ali died; they said Ali will come back. They started saying everyone that comes from the progeny of Ali, they're called 12 imams, and those 12 imams know everything. Those 12 imams know the unseen, they will judge with Allah, they're infallible. They started making up beliefs.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Questioned On Sectarianism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MnwLenfsZWA", ((520, "8:40–9:27"),))
