#passage(("The main difference between Sunnis and Shias, when it comes to the subject of beliefs, it's where we get these beliefs. It's based on our sources that we have different beliefs. Our historical perspective [is] also based on our sources. Our mannerisms are also based on our sources, and that's why sources are so important. So, to give you guys an example: when it comes to Shiaism, one of the main foundations is the belief in 12 imams. The Imam is an infallible, divinely appointed person; that role is to guide Humanity. And if you reject one of the imams, then you're ultimately, unfortunately, going to end up in Hell forever. That's a belief; that's what [Shias are] believing, and this belief is not something that you could ever arrive [at] if you were someone that exclusively took from Sunni sources.", "These differences influence everything about our Islam, so it's very important to look into these sources and compare these sources, to come to an awareness as to why we follow these sources. One more example: if you're going to look at the characters from Sunni sources, you can have a pro-[Uthman] view; you'd have a positive opinion of [Uthman]. Again, we're all bound to our sources.",), "Farid Responds, “Why are Sunnis and Shia Different? Full Breakdown (AIM Conference)”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Un_bX5Zm3o0", ((112, "1:52–3:56"), (274, "4:34–5:12"),))
// U FR094:16-49 | Farid Responds | 1
#passage(("You said that we're very influenced by communities. And to continue this idea: our communities, they're influenced by the scholars, and the scholars, they're influenced by scholars. It goes all the way back to the two sets of primary sources. We got the [six]; [Shia], they got the four books from the three Muhammads. Which of these two should we stick with? Because ultimately, if you think about it, if the [Shia] didn't have the [Shia] books, and they were stuck with the six books and whatnot, they wouldn't be believing the 12 imams, that the last one is hidden for [1,200] years in occultation. No one would believe this. You need the [Shia] books to believe in this. Similarly, if the Sunnis didn't have the Sunni works, and they only had the four books of the Shia and whatnot, naturally the Sunnis would have a very negative view of the sahabah, and they would be believing in the 12 imams and all of that.",), "Farid Responds, “Eid Message & Gift to Ammar Nakshawani”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eSbnXLfMR6w", ((47, "0:47–2:07"),))
