#passage(("Let's talk briefly about Ghadir Khum. In Ghadir Khum, it says that upon you is the Book of Allah, and they'd say Ahl alBayt. Another thing, which is a very important belief of the Shi'a: it says that you have to follow Ahl alBayt. This is in creed. A part of your creed is you have to follow Ahl alBayt. So, in Ghadir Khum, it says the first thing is the Book of Allah. Upon you is, first, the Book of Allah. So we start with the Book of Allah. They say this narration is the most important narration. So we're going to use that narration. The narration says: upon you is the Book of Allah, first. So let's focus on the Book of Allah. We and the Shi'a agree on the Book of Allah. This is the common ground that we have. We both say we believe in the same book. The majority of the Shi'a would say we believe in all of it is from God: the one that we have, they say they believe it's from God. So, if we agree that this Book is from Allah, now let's use this Book and see: is this Book in agreement to the beliefs of the Shi'a that we highlighted or not?", "You say you believe in the Quran, and we believe in the Quran; we believe in the same Book. This Book is from God. It's God's Revelation. It's Guidance for mankind. Allah says in the Quran (alAn'am6:38) مَّا فَرَّطْنَا فِي الْكِتَابِ مِن شَيْءٍ: we did not leave anything out of this Book. This is referring to اللوح المحفوظ (al Lawh alMahfudh: The Preserved Tablet) actually. But generally, Allah says that this book is guidance for all areas of life. If it doesn't give you specific details, it'll give you principles, like follow the Prophet, for instance. So it'll give you principles which would lead you into all areas of life. But this book is guidance for mankind, so it should guide you and me. We're having a disagreement now. Allah says in that same Book فَإِن تَنَـٰزَعۡتُمۡ فِی شَیۡءࣲ فَرُدُّوهُ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَٱلرَّسُولِ (anNisa4:59) (If you disagree over anything, [then] return it to the Quran and the Prophet). So we start first with the Quran. So, if it says to return it to Allah, referring to the Quran, and then the Prophet, that is fair. And they should not say it's not fair, because they are saying we believe in the Quran, the Quran is from God's Revelation, all of that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Fully Dismantles The Shia Position! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t7vhKiTrvNA", ((480, "8:00–9:18"), (585, "9:45–10:48"),))
