#passage(("The second thing I'm going to say, responding to what you said about the Quran, that it requires interpretation: that is YOUR false belief. The Quran explicitly says there's clear verses in the Quran, and there are ambiguous verses. So there are two types of verses. Allah says in the Quran in chapter:3 (alImran), verse:7, about the Quran: مِنۡهُ ءَایَـٰتࣱ مُّحۡكَمَـٰتٌ هُنَّ أُمُّ ٱلۡكِتَـٰبِ (From it are foundational verses): clear-cut verses are found in the Quran. Allah says (alIkhlas112:1) قُلۡ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ أَحَدٌ (say Allah is uniquely one). Clear verse! And there are verses which are ambiguous, but then Allah tells us how to interpret them. Allah says in the Quran (anNahl16:64) that the Messenger is sent to explain these verses, to teach us حِكمَة (Hikma: wisdom) (alBaqara2:151). Allah says what? The Prophet! Allah says (anNahl16:44) وَأَنزَلۡنَاۤ إِلَیۡكَ ٱلذِّكۡرَ لِتُبَیِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ مَا نُزِّلَ إِلَیۡهِمۡ (We sent down to you the Dhikr so you can explain to the people the Quran). Allah says in the Quran (alAhzab33:21) لَّقَدۡ كَانَ لَكُمۡ فِی رَسُولِ ٱللَّهِ أُسۡوَةٌ حَسَنَةࣱ (You have in the Messenger of Allah a great example). Allah tells us in the Quran (alImran3:164) that He sent us the Prophet to teach us the Quran and the Hikma (wisdom). So all of these are verses telling us that the Prophet is going to teach us the meaning of the Quran.", "Now, your false creed teaches two things. First, it teaches the existence of the Imams and the unseen or whatever. Then you have your own false عَقِيدة (‘Aqida: creed), which is a ‘Aqida of بَاطِنيّة (Bateniyya: Esotericism): that the Quran has an internal meaning that only the Imams know. So go ahead, show me one single verse! Where does the Quran mention the Imams? Or say that we need to get our religion and understanding of the Quran from the Imams? So Allah, in 6,000 verses, told us the Prophet, everywhere, in tens of verses, is going to teach us the Quran. But He didn't send us one single verse that actually tells us: the interpretation is actually with the Imams, it's not with the Prophet! So where is that verse in the Quran? Bring me one verse, or simply say, I don't have it. Either bring me one verse in the Quran: mentions the Imams, anything to do with the Imams, that the knowledge of the religion is taken from the Imams, anything! One verse from the Quran! This is every Shi'a that you're going to talk to. They have nothing to present for their own main creed in the Quran. Nothing! There is a reason Shi'as are a minority.", "Then she says that maybe things have been altered. So I'm going to ask you this question now: are you saying the Quran is corrupted? Yes or no? By the way, either way, whatever you say is not going to help you, because you have 2000 narrations in your book, in alKafi, that talk about the corruption of the Quran. So you disagree with these scholars that mentioned these narrations; that doesn't matter, the narrations are there!", "Now, I'm going to say something very simple. Whether you say the Quran is corrupted or not, you're still shooting yourself in the foot. If you say the Quran is corrupted, then you're shooting yourself in the foot, because the Quran says it's not corrupted, and then you're a disbeliever, because you're saying the Book of Allah is corrupted. Or you say, no, it's not corrupted, and then you can explain how your most important creed in the religion, the 12 Imams, the fact that they're infallible, the fact that they should exist at every time, the fact that they're divinely appointed, the fact that only they have the interpretation of the Quran, all of these things, which are the whole religion, your whole religion is based on, you don’t have even a single verse in an uncorrupted Quran that talks about that?? So now explain to me why there isn't even a single verse that talks about the great foundation of your faith? You agree with me that if someone doesn't believe in the Imama (authority of Imam), in the 12 Imams, he’s a disbeliever in your faith. So something that is in your faith that makes you a disbeliever: why is there not even a single verse about it in the Quran?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Shia Girl Confronts Muslim On His Claims Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LcbjBQElXe0", ((419, "6:59–8:04"), (488, "8:08–10:00"), (628, "10:28–11:05"), (667, "11:07–12:03"),))
