#passage(("How we pray? The Prophetﷺ, we believe he said: \"pray as you see me pray\". Who's around him seeing him pray? It were the Companions! We have their description of how he prayed, and we pray that way. Every Book that you see, the books of narrations of the Shi'a, comes hundreds of years after, because they don't come from those people, because they don't accept them. None of them are reliable sources for us to say that they trace back to the Prophetﷺ. So we don't need to accept any of them. And they attribute lies to them. And even their own narrations, they'd agree that there are liars in these narrations, but they will still use them. They will agree they're not authentic narrations; they will still use them. There isn't a single narration that is authentic that is identifying the Imam that is alive today, and who he is, and where he is, and all of these things. There isn't. They will tell you this is an unknown person. He's there. He's just divinely appointed. And he's not leading anyone, but he's an Imam, come on!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Fully Dismantles The Shia Position! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t7vhKiTrvNA", ((2662, "44:22–45:21"),))
