#passage(("You told me an example for praying on the Turba. Go ahead and present me in Bukhari and Muslim: where is that proof that you can pray on the Turba, on the dirt or the sand or whatever? That doesn't prove your point, because your Turba is specific to the death of Hussein. It's not just any random dust or dirt. It's specific, from a specific location, related to a specific event. If you want to bring in a narration, it has to specifically say that, because you have a specific Turba that you use from a specific location. What's the evidence for that specific Turba, from the Shia books even? Leave the Sunni books. Why are the overwhelming majority doing it? And if you go to your Shia scholar, he would not tell you this is wrong. He would tell you, yes, it's a blessed Turba because Hussein died. That's what he's going to tell you. But go ask him for the evidence: nothing. No evidence.", "Whatever you're going to present, whatever disagreement you have between Ahlu-sSunnah and the Shia, you're not going to be able to present evidences for it. Definitely from the Quran, you're not going to find anything. But even from the books of Ahlu-sSunnah, you can ONLY TWIST things to try and do something. And they will tell you that's in Bukhari and Muslim. But I'll tell you the truth is, you didn't go and look, because the overwhelming majority that they tell you is in our books is not really in our books.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Shia Follower Gets An Unexpected Reality Check! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6v8T06xoukk", ((1143, "19:03–20:40"), (1242, "20:42–21:03"),))
