#passage(("It's all political, and there's people from the lineage, so their beliefs are all related to that. And they also beat themselves! On the date the grandson of the Prophetﷺ died, they beat themselves. Why are you beating yourself? The Quran says do not harm yourself! It's an emotional thing that they have. They're attached emotionally to an event that happened in history, with someone who's been killed, martyred. And whenever that date comes, emotionally they just beat themselves: oh, we need to feel the same pain that he felt.", "The Shias, they would agree with us [on] the same Quran. Only thing we're going to say to them: look, chapter 4 verse 59 says, when you disagree, go back to the Quran and Hadith. Where is in the Quran the beliefs that you're bringing? They will agree that none of these beliefs are in the Quran, because it's not there! It's an objective reality; it's not about agreeing or disagreeing. You open the Quran: show me, where is the 12 imams that will come and will be infallible, and we should follow them? There's no such thing.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Skeptical About The Prophet of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QIxWrKc_J_Y", ((2438, "40:38–41:30"), (2508, "41:48–42:07"),))
