=== 44.8 Wilayah takwiniyyah and the powers of the Imams
// NODE P11.C03.S08
#author("Farid Responds")
// U FR057:362-465 | Farid Responds | 2
#passage(("The whole thing gets worse when [Haqiqatjou] has a discussion with [Adnan Rashid] just a few days ago. [He] presents three versions: the first, meaning that Allah stepped aside from the matters of the universe after giving the imams full control and authority over all the atoms in the universe. The second view simply means that they're able to perform miracles, and the third view is that the imams, they just make Dua and their Dua is always accepted. But he says that the two other views fall in line with Sunnism.", "Now we have a little problem here, because [he] has actually left out the correct definition, and he's provided three other definitions. And by the way, this isn't just me saying it: the deceased wrote a book on this subject, and he rejected the other definitions. So for example, the ability to perform miracles: we all believe, all Muslims believe, even non-Muslims believe, that there are people that were able to perform miracles, and therefore, due to this, we find it farfetched that the above is the intended meaning by its proponents; in fact, it is against the clear statements. We also doubt that what is meant is the acceptance of supplications. He then provides the fifth explanation, which says Allah handed over the [reins] of the universe to them; he granted them full authority over all the components of the universe, and they may do as they please. If they wish to add anything, they may add it, and if they wish to remove anything, they have all the power to do so. They may change sunrise from the east to the west, and they may remove the mountains. [He] refutes this by saying the Quran contradicts this; however, he says, unfortunately the proponents build upon the fifth possibility. This is the correct definition.",), "Farid Responds, “Haqiqatjou is a Shirk Apologist”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nQExb2jL7uY", ((984, "16:24–19:35"), (1175, "19:35–21:23"),))
// U FR057:333-361 | Farid Responds | 1
#passage(("First of all, Hijab never agreed that independence is a condition for one being upon [shirk], as Jake was able to prove. Daniel initially started off by saying there are Sunnis that believe [in wilayah]; now he's saying you can't make [takfir] of those that place a condition of dependence on Allah when they hold the view.",), "Farid Responds, “Haqiqatjou is a Shirk Apologist”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nQExb2jL7uY", ((906, "15:06–16:01"),))
// U FR057:466-587 | Farid Responds | 3
#passage(("This version, which is the correct definition, is the definition that has been expressing in the past, but all of a sudden, during his discussion with [Adnan] Rashid, he pretends that this definition doesn't exist. So what happened? Why were you expressing this view in the past, this meaning, and now you pretend that it doesn't exist, and you've substituted it with three different definitions?", "[Fadlallah] is talking about himself. He's not saying [Shia] don't believe in this; there are some [Shia] that believe in this, and that's why he wrote his book: it's to refute this. Then he quotes \"we don't believe in this\" as proof that [Shia] don't believe in this. He's refuting this concept that was adopted by some major [Shia].", "Your footnote mentions nothing about Dua. Let's read, when speaking about the [wilayah] of the imams: it is a [wilayah] pertaining to the whole of creation, by virtue of which all of the atoms in the universe humble themselves before the authority [of] the holder. Anything about [tafwid] there? No. Anything about Dua there? No.",), "Farid Responds, “Haqiqatjou is a Shirk Apologist”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nQExb2jL7uY", ((1284, "21:24–21:59"), (1357, "22:37–23:27"), (1535, "25:35–26:02"),))

=== 44.9 Shia works on the biography of the Prophet
// NODE P11.C03.S09
#author("Farid Responds")
// U FR095:16-149 | Farid Responds | 4
#passage(("He is presenting something very important which is often overlooked: the differences between Muhammad in [Shia] works and in Sunni works, and should we stick with the [Shia] biography for the prophet or should we stick with the Sunni biographies? It's a very important question, and there's a major issue. What are the [Shia] works of [sirah] that you want us to go back to in order to learn about the prophet peace be upon him? Don't you know that sunnis have a monopoly?", "I got a bunch of books of [sirah], all of course Sunni works of [sirah], and alhamdulillah I'm really happy to have that. It's a blessing to know about the [sirah] of the Prophet peace be upon him. But what about [Shia] books? These are all [Shia] works, that's 30 volumes. What I'm trying to say is I got a lot of [Shia] books. [Shia] authors don't care about the [sirah] of the Prophet peace be upon him; they care about the [sirah] of the imams. Masallah, they really do care about the [sirah] of the imams. It's about the narrations of everything about all the [imams], but the prophet peace be upon him, I don't have anything. I got these, the closest thing I have; he's from the sixth Century. These Works actually rely on Sunni works.", "So here he Praises Alim, he says he's one of our best narrators, and he says this: when he became 37 years old he sees in his dream that someone would come to him and would say: oh prophet of Allah, oh messenger of Allah, and the prophet peace be upon him would deny this. And then when he was [herding] some sheep for his uncle Abu Talib, he saw a person, and he said: who are you? So this shows, according to your own source, that the prophet peace be upon him did not believe that he was a prophet initially.", "But what I also find interesting is both of these texts actually rely on [Sunni] sources quite heavily. The reality is the most important [Shia] sources on the biography of the Prophet rely on Sunni sources. You're saying we have a narrative of him first receiving the Revelation. It's very easy to criticize the Sunni version of events, but why don't you provide us with the [Shia] version of events? Don't just say he was always a prophet, he's been praying since before he was born, or something like that, or [Jibril] asks him: can I recite to you [al-Fatiha]?",), "Farid Responds, “The Real Prophet of Islam - Response to Ammar Nakshawani”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZXc-9xL3DNs", ((40, "0:40–1:20"), (126, "2:06–3:22"), (277, "4:37–5:34"), (338, "5:38–6:41"),))
// U FR095:262-280 | Farid Responds | 1
#passage(("I know that you're watching my videos. You don't have to mention me by name, just drop a hint, slip it in there: a [sirah] book, a book that you'd recommend. You can say: some people, they ask me to present a [sirah] book, and this is one I strongly recommend. I will happily read whatever you have to recommend.",), "Farid Responds, “The Real Prophet of Islam - Response to Ammar Nakshawani”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZXc-9xL3DNs", ((694, "11:34–11:57"),))

== 45. Sectarianism and Muslim unity

=== 45.1 Why Muslims are divided into sects
// NODE P11.C04.S01
#author("The Muslim Lantern")
// U ML364:2-23 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("I would say: enter the house. Once you enter the house, look at the furniture. Can I look at the furniture without entering the house? No, I have to enter the house. So if you want to look at different sects, which can be in this analogy furniture, you have to enter into the house of Islam first. Once you enter the house of Islam, you look at it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Questioned On Sectarianism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MnwLenfsZWA", ((26, "0:26–0:48"),))
// U ML347:711-754 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("Allah عزوجل said that he will test us with division. He commanded us not to be divided. Allah clearly says in the Quran3:103: وَٱعۡتَصِمُوا۟ بِحَبۡلِ ٱللَّهِ جَمِیعࣰا وَلَا تَفَرَّقُوا۟ۚ \"And hold on tight to the rope of Allah -which is the Quran- and do not get divided. And remember the blessing of Allah upon you when you were divided and he gathered you.\" He made you united at the beginning! So do not get divided. Allah says: (إِنَّ الَّذِينَ فَرَّقُوا دِينَهُمْ وَكَانُوا شِيَعًا لَّسْتَ مِنْهُمْ فِي شَيْءٍ) (Quran6:159). He says to the Prophet: \"those who divide the religions and become sects and groups, you are free from them.\"", "Allah says: (وَمَن يُشَاقِقِ الرَّسُولَ مِن بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ الْهُدَىٰ وَيَتَّبِعْ غَيْرَ سَبِيلِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ) Quran4:115, \"The one who opposes the Messenger after guidance have been made clear to him and go against the way of the believers.\" So the believers have a way, but there will be people who will go against the way of the believers. But Allah has given us a principle. He said how we can know where the Truth is: \"if you disagree over anything, returning to Allah and the Messenger\" (Quran4:59). And Allah says to us that the examples for us to follow are the Companions, in chapter 9 verse 100, because they learn directly from the Prophet.", "Now Allah also says in the Quran6:65 (Alan'aam) (قُلْ هُوَ الْقَادِرُ عَلَىٰ أَن يَبْعَثَ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابًا) that \"he is the one who is able to send upon you a punishment, that he will make you scattered and divided.\" And he will make you fight one another even, taste the harshness of one another, as a punishment! So division can be a punishment, can be a test for the people, because this life is a test, and there will be people who will choose to twist parts of the religion they don't agree with, to follow their own desires and do whatever they want to do.", "And the Prophet told us 1400 years ago that this أمة Ummah, this Nation, will be divided into 73 sects, so us seeing the division is proof that Islam is the Truth. Because if there was unity, then that doesn't make any sense, because the Prophet told us there will be division.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Challenges Muslim On God Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MSk1AiEaXH8", ((2125, "35:25–35:54"), (2163, "36:03–36:36"), (2202, "36:42–37:07"), (2260, "37:40–37:51"),))
// R quran_003_103.json
#refbox("Reference text: Quran 3:103, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("3:103", "And hold firmly to the rope of Allāh all together and do not become divided. And remember the favor of Allāh upon you - when you were enemies and He brought your hearts together and you became, by His favor, brothers. And you were on the edge of a pit of the Fire, and He saved you from it. Thus does Allāh make clear to you His verses that you may be guided."),))
// R quran_006_159.json
#refbox("Reference text: Quran 6:159, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("6:159", "Indeed, those who have divided their religion and become sects - you, [O Muḥammad], are not [associated] with them in anything. Their affair is only [left] to Allāh; then He will inform them about what they used to do."),))
// R quran_004_115.json
#refbox("Reference text: Quran 4:115, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("4:115", "And whoever opposes the Messenger after guidance has become clear to him and follows other than the way of the believers - We will give him what he has taken and drive him into Hell, and evil it is as a destination."),))
