#passage(("It's not really about the sects, it's about your beliefs. So for example, he can say I’m Ahmadi, or a person can come to me and say I’m Shia, but what he believes is not really what the Shias believe in their books. He says he's Ahmadi because he was born in an Ahmadi family; that's why he's saying he's Ahmadi. I know he's not done enough research to look at the Sunni position and look at the difference between it and the Ahmadi position. So a lot of people would say I’m Ahmadi, but they're not really on the beliefs of Ahmadis. A lot of people will say I’m Shia, but they're not on the beliefs of Shia. Point is, when I talk to him, he should agree with me that whatever is in the Quran is what he and me should believe, both of us.", "The Quran itself says that. If you have any disagreements, you have to return it to the Quran4:59: “O you who believe, obey Allah, obey the Messenger and those in authority among you. And if you disagree over anything, refer it to Allah”, which is the Quran, “and the Messenger”, which is his literature, the Hadith, “if you believe in Allah and the Last Day.” Allah is saying: if you believe in Me, and you believe in the Last Day, then do this; this is the best way.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Questioned On Sectarianism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MnwLenfsZWA", ((212, "3:32–4:12"), (268, "4:28–5:06"),))
