#passage(("The fact that there are different people, some of which correctly interpreted the text and some of which incorrectly interpret the text, does not change the reality that this text is from God. I'll give you an example: there are different teachers who can teach you how to swim; that does not mean teaching how to swim now is an incorrect concept. So just because different people who are reading the Quran or the text are coming to different conclusions, assuming this is the case, it doesn't mean that this is not from God.", "So when you talk about different [sects], if you want to use that term, the Quran is very clear on how you understand it. Now anyone who doesn't follow what the Quran teaches you of how to understand it, by definition, will exclude these people from being people who are following the guidance. The Quran has principles. Anyone who comes and tells me anything that is against the Quran explicitly or the Hadith, I'm going to reject it. I don't need to accept that. The Quran itself, which is what we're supposed to be coming back to as Muslims, is telling me to keep this as the authority.", "The Quran says the companions of the Prophet are the ones we follow, their description and their righteousness. Allah says that in chapter 9 [verse] 100: that if you follow these companions, Allah is pleased with you, because he's pleased with them, and he's prepared Paradise for you. So me following the Companions and righteousness is going to lead me to attaining Eternal Paradise. As Allah says in the Quran, the prophet is the one who explains the Quran. As Allah says in chapter 16 of the Quran: so you can clarify to the people that which was revealed to them. So the prophet is the example; Allah says in the Quran as well: you have the example in the prophet. So how do we understand the Quran? Through the life of the Prophet, through his companions, which you supposed to follow, because he told them how to live the life.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Pakistani Ex-Muslim Confronts A Muslim On Following Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9vJWVgYof2A", ((774, "12:54–13:22"), (802, "13:22–14:03"), (843, "14:03–14:46"),))
