#refbox("Reference text: Quran 9:100, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("9:100", "And the first forerunners [in the faith] among the Muhājireen and the Anṣār and those who followed them with good conduct - Allāh is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him, and He has prepared for them gardens beneath which rivers flow, wherein they will abide forever. That is the great attainment."),))
// U ML041:94-132 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Within Christianity, there isn't any text that tells you how to interpret the Bible. There isn't any text that tells you, if you disagree on a understanding, how to solve it. But in the Quran, it's explicitly stated, chapter 4: what to do when you disagree. We separate between God's words and people's words. So if someone comes and says: \"Is it okay to do X?\" I'm a Muslim saying: \"No, it's not okay.\" Another Muslim says: \"It's okay.\" What does the Quran say? What does the prophet say? So we have a way to return things back into the tradition.", "Now, with Christian groups, for instance, Protestants would say we have something called sola scriptura, only the scriptures, solely the scriptures. Sola scriptura is one of the creeds of being a Protestant. But if you go to the Catholics and the Orthodox, you look at the church fathers and the church: we can believe what they say even if it goes against the Bible. So it's not only the scripture. We can take our religion not only from the scripture, but we can also take it from the church fathers, can take it from the pope, because he's infallible, he's God's representative on Earth. So these are major differences. And every Christian I talk to, literally every Christian I talk to, has a different belief. Not two Christians have ever been identical, and I talked to thousands of them.", "And the issue is something like the Trinity. It doesn't enter the human mind. The reason it doesn't enter the human mind is because it's a made-up concept. It's not truly from God. It's impossible for human mind to comprehend something that is a made-up concept, philosophical concept. And that's why every Christian would have a different way of explaining it, depending on what they heard in the church or whatever their mind came up with as an understanding.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Couple Ask A Muslim To Explain World Suffering! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9AACeXB0A9Q", ((215, "3:35–4:33"), (273, "4:33–5:19"), (321, "5:21–5:47"),))
// U ML364:230-290 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("When you look at all those types of sects that you said, the point is they're not following what the Quran is teaching. And you can bring any of them and I’ll talk to them; I showed him the verse and I’ll say the same thing to them. And I got many people who come who are Ahmadis, and what happens is they never come back. They say to me: I’m not knowledgeable, I’ll bring you a scholar. I say: bring a scholar, and they never come back. I don't see a scholar, I don't see anyone, and I am here, I am always here.", "So the point is this: we will all be on one belief if we hold onto the Quran. So what Allah says in the Quran: \"Hold on tight to the rope of Allah\", which is the Quran and the Prophet, “and do not get divided.” Allah is telling us: “and remember the blessing of Allah upon you; in the beginning you were disagreeing and then the Prophet united you.” Quran3:103. So Allah is saying to us: do not get divided, hold on tight to the Quran and to the Prophet. What some people do: they ignore what the Quran says, they ignore what the Prophet says, and they start making their own traditions and their own beliefs. These sects are deviations; they are people who are not following the Quran and Hadith properly. So anyone who follows the Quran and Hadith properly will be fine, will be good on the Day of Judgement. Muslim! That's the name for the people who follow the Quran and Sunnah that way; that should be their name. Ahmadis call themselves Ahmadi. They attribute themselves to their Prophet, Ghulam Ahmad.", "There's the beautiful tradition of Prophet Muhammad. One of his companions was called Hudhaifah Ibn Alyaman. He said to the Prophet: \"Oh Prophet of Allah\" -because in the future there will be trials and tribulations and people who will be divided- so he asked the Prophet: \"what should I do?\" He said: “hold onto the group of the Muslims.” He said to him: “what if there's no group?” He said: “hold onto the leader.” \"If there's no leader?\" The Prophet عليه الصلاة والسلام said: leave all the groups, leave all the sects, just hold on tight to what the Quran and Sunnah tell you.", "So the more the division is there, the Prophet told us what to do is to come back to the Quran and to the Sunnah. So we have to follow the Quran, the Prophet and the Companions, how they understood the Quran. So if someone comes to me and says this verse means this, I’ll say: which Companion said that? If he doesn't have a Companion, I’ll say what you're saying doesn't make sense, because the Quran told me to follow the Companions. So anyone who believes in the Quran and the Sunnah and follows it in the Companions’ understanding, like the Quran teaches you, he will not get misguided. And there are many people who are believing that; many people are on the Right Path. What is the population of Muslims? 99% of the population of Muslims are not Ahmadi, and they don't believe Ahmadis are Muslims.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Questioned On Sectarianism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MnwLenfsZWA", ((665, "11:05–11:26"), (689, "11:29–12:43"), (775, "12:55–13:21"), (807, "13:27–14:14"),))
