// U ML239:1218-1309 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("There are people who say, we follow the righteous predecessors, we have name X, and they have this big name on a [billboard]: I'm part of that group and we have this huge name; come to my group; if you're not from my group, then you're misguided. You have to be from my group, you sit with me here, you listen to me, or you're misguided; you take from my scholar or you're misguided; you listen to me or you're not upon the truth; we're the only people upon the truth, come to us, our Masjid, our people.", "Then we having issues here. If I have the truth, then it's incumbent upon me to have goodness for other people. None of you will become a Believer until he loves for his brother [what] he loves for himself. You give a name to yourself, whatever that name is, and you say, I'm the safe person and everyone else is misguided. If you find people doing this, certain groups doing this, stay away from them. You'll hear this a lot: yesterday he didn't shave his armpit, therefore he's a person of misguidance, don't sit down with him. If you hear too many of these things, then be aware there's some fishy business going on.", "What is the name? We said we're not giving any names to ourselves. What is the name that we all give to ourselves and we have to give to ourselves? It is Muslim. The prophet, he said, name yourself, for Allah named you, the Muslim, the servant of Allah. These are the names you give to yourself: you are a Muslim.", "Now someone will come and say, okay, but everyone says I'm a Muslim. Yes, everyone says I'm a Muslim, but not everyone believes the same thing. If you see what they believe, you listen to them: are they using Quran and Sunnah? So they can call themselves potato for all I care. It doesn't matter what you call yourself, because you can say, okay, I'm going to call my sect the great people; we are the great people. If you have this person here start say, I'm from the great people, does it mean now he's become from the great people? We look at what is the attributes of these people, what do they believe, and then we look: does he have the same beliefs as these people, does he do the same actions? This is how you identify the people upon the truth, not by names, name calling: what you believe, what you speak about and what you preach to other people.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((2823, "47:03–47:39"), (2859, "47:39–48:31"), (2911, "48:31–49:23"), (2963, "49:23–50:16"),))
// U ML248:2702-2744 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("When we say you call yourself Muslim, some people, they come and say, but everyone calls themselves Muslim. But the same can apply for any name you call yourself: you can call yourself [Salafi], everyone can call themselves [Salafi], doesn't mean they are. So you just be a Muslim, follow the correct beliefs.", "That's why they started using this name later on for specific group, so they can say this is just [Imam] Ahmed's belief, it's not everyone's belief. So it was a way to distinguish: okay, we follow this [Imam], you follow that [Imam]. It's not about any [Imams], it's about the Quran [and Sunnah]. They were upon this belief. Why were they associated with the Creed? Because they were the Forefront of Defending it. It's not about the individual; that's why I never tied to an individual. It's all about what do they represent, what did they defend, and that is what you have to be upon.", "Today we have brothers saying salafi, and they couldn't name 10 sahabah. This is such a sad state that we live in. Go learn and follow, bring it into your life. Today you have a brother that won't say Salam to you because you were sitting with another brother. Were they like this? Did they stop Salam to each other? It's ridiculous.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Amazing Collab| The Muslim Lantern & Sheikh Uthman Meet For The First Time| @OneMessageFoundation”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LVdIHlFWDgc", ((6403, "1:46:43–1:47:03"), (6426, "1:47:06–1:47:46"), (6467, "1:47:47–1:48:13"),))
