#passage(("First and foremost, you ask Allah for guidance. Prophet Muhammad, who's the best among us all: Allah says in the Quran, if we did not give you firmness, you would have inclined towards the disbelievers a little bit. That's why the prophet, one of the [du'a] he used to say the most: oh Turner of Hearts, keep my heart firm on your religion. Because the most important thing to know is that the firm establishment is from Allah.", "Secondly, you look at the people, as we said, who say we are upon the same beliefs; they're proud to say this: we are upon the same beliefs as the righteous predecessors. But they will also be upon an implementation. They're not going to be like, these people are bad, don't go sit down with this, only our [masjid] you can pray. There's a warning here: we're not talking about these ones. They don't believe they're a sect, from what sense? From the sense is that they excommunicate everyone else: just us, we're the only ones who are winning. So you look for these people who are proud to call themselves this, and they are not controversial: the scholars, they're praising them, they're okay with them; you don't see them engaging back and forth with each other. And there's many of today, many in other parts of the lands as well, all over the world, and they're not only in one region.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((9931, "2:45:31–2:46:16"), (9979, "2:46:19–2:47:33"),))

