#passage(("There's a lot more disagreements between Sunni and Shia. In the beginning, in the start, yes, you can say it started with this idea that who should have been the successor of The Prophetﷺ (peace and blessings be upon him) after his death. But later on, it's become an entire religion with a new set of beliefs. And it's not just about 'Ali being the successor. They said that his entire lineage, there must be someone from his lineage: you have the 12 people – 12 Imams (Spiritual Leaders), and that you have it each time, you need to have a representative appointed by God as the leader of the Muslims, and he has to be from the lineage of The Prophetﷺ, which is not Islamic and not from The Quran and Sunnah, hence why they are a small minority.", "It's definitely not accurate to say there's just one small disagreement. There's more disagreements about the Companions of The Prophet, about the wives of The Prophet, and certain beliefs to do with infallibility with people, knowing the unseen and stuff like that. There's a lot more differences that arose later on; it's not as simple as just about 'Ali ؓ (RadiyAllahu 'anhu: May Allah be pleased with him).", "There are many groups of people who believe in different things. But in reality, all Muslims believe in the same Quran, believe in the same Prophet, believe in the same God. So unlike other religions, where the differences in belief will be big differences in theology, in who's God, who's not God, and the number of books that they follow and issues like that, it's not the case when it comes to Muslims. These, if you want to use the term sects, their disagreements are not going to [be core] foundation level, like, for example, a different Quran, different numbers of books in The Quran and issues like that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Responding To Professor Jiang's Lecture On The Islamic Golden Age | Muhammed Ali!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6SVGKQ-xiGs", ((238, "3:58–4:35"), (280, "4:40–5:01"), (318, "5:18–5:44"),))
// U ML340:223-254 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("Now this idea of division of Sunni and Shia: the word \"Shia\" itself in the Arabic language means \"a group\", aligning to a group, or being from a group, or a group of people, that's it! And the word \"Sunni\" means: to follow the Sunnah, which is the way of the Prophet Muhammad, what he did in his life; you actually behave the way he behaved. So, that's what the word means.", "Some people have this perception that 50% of Muslims are Sunni, 50% percent of Muslim are Shia; No! You got less than 10% of the population of Muslims in the world, they are Shia. And within Shiism, you've got different sects as well, who believe different things.", "Where does it come from? It was a political disagreement that happened after the death of Prophet Muhammad. There was two individuals who disagreed. It was that one individual who was killed, a group of people, they wanted the retribution for him, and the other group of people, they said, wait, not now. So, there was this disagreement. Then the group of people who aligned themselves with the person, they were called Shia, and the other group, who just said OK let's wait, or every other Muslim, is what we call Sunni.", "So, it's a political issue that is not really impacting our day-to-day life as Muslims. If you see Muslims when they live their day-to-day life, they don't think much about Sunni or Shia. Let's go to pray: they pray, they follow the Quran, they do the teachings of God, and that's it, because they understand this was a political issue. The important thing is that we stick to the teachings of the Quran. So we will have a problem with any group, or any sect, if they go against the teachings. But if you're following the teachings, then we're happy; you can call yourself whatever you want to call yourself.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Audience Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=imKsFyzx-Yo", ((889, "14:49–15:03"), (907, "15:07–15:18"), (922, "15:22–15:43"), (949, "15:49–16:16"),))
// U ML311:244-346 | The Muslim Lantern | 6
#passage(("I'd advise not to get into that; that's what I generally advise. Because as a new Muslim, you should focus on the foundations of the faith, not on the things that are branches that people might disagree about. As long as you don't do certain things that some Shias do. Like, for example, would you pray to a dead person? Ask help from a dead person? Would you beat yourself because someone was killed someday, you start beating yourself up?", "The question is: how can someone worship a cow? How can someone not just worship a cow, but literally eat the excrement that comes out of a cow! Why does that happen? is the question. Some of these people have PHDs, they went to space according to them. So why would they do these things? It's Pantheism. They believe that everything is god, including the cows, including everything in Creation. So they believe these things are actually god.", "Let me explain how it happens in Shia circles. If you're born in Shia cultural tradition, you're born and the whole religion for you has nothing to do with the Prophetﷺ, has nothing to do with following the Quran, has nothing to do with following the Hadith. The whole religion for you is about what happened between two individuals in history, about leadership! This is the whole religion for you! The whole religion for you is to curse some of the Companions of the Prophet, to curse the wife of the Prophetﷺ. The whole religion for you is to call upon the cousin of the Prophetﷺ, who is dead, and ask him for help and seek aid from him, and believe he has Supernatural powers, and believe he cannot do anything wrong and he's never done anything wrong. This is what they're taught since they're young.", "So the thing is, they're not taught Islam to begin with! Therefore it's not that they have understood the crystal clear idea of Islam. If you bring me Shias now, I'll show you they don't know anything about the Quran, nothing! If they were reading Quran, they wouldn't curse the Companions, because The Quran praises the Companions. If they were reading the Quran, they cannot say anything about the wife of the Prophetﷺ, because the Prophetﷺ says they are our Mothers. So, if they were reading Quran, they’ll understand that they need to follow the Companions.", "The fact is, they don't read the Quran, and their “Scholars”, there are many videos of them on YouTube where they are not able to read basic Surahs of the Quran. The first few Surahs, they are not able to read them, they're making mistakes; these are Scholars of the Shias, they're not normal ones, they’re Scholars. So when you've got people have been raised upon complete ignorance, upon emotional stories, wherever they’re told in every Jumaa’ (Friday) prayer, they tell them a story when one of the Companions of the Prophetﷺ, he killed the daughter of the Prophetﷺ: this fake story that they made up! This is the religion for them. This is literally it! And in their books, if you read, the religion for them is to oppose the people of Ahl As-Sunnah, that's it! There's no religion or follow the Quran, follow the Hadith; that's not their religion.", "It's much deeper than that, but I'm just giving you a basic point of view now of how it is, and what it is, the understanding that they follow. That's why I said I don't want to get you too much into, so you don't get confused by this and that. You focus on the Quran and following the Prophetﷺ; that should be more than enough for you.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Man Realises The Contradictions In Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CR6_RG9qdVM", ((971, "16:11–16:31"), (1038, "17:18–17:58"), (1101, "18:21–18:59"), (1144, "19:04–19:23"), (1168, "19:28–20:05"), (1220, "20:20–20:34"),))
