#passage(("A lot of people want to [harp] on a lot of division, and a lot of people want to do unity. We have two sides of people: you have people who want to unite and you have people who want to cause division between people. But we need to understand: when we say unite, there must be something that we unite on. You can just say unite. Okay, unite on what? There must be something that we unite on.", "It's very important to keep this point of mind. There's a lot of people who go on the extreme side, calling disbelievers and whatever, and that's not the right thing to do and that's not correct. This has never been a proper scholarly position in the Sunni school. If you go to the books, if you go to scholars, they don't blanket say that the Shia are disbelievers. This is not a position that we hold. I believe personally the overwhelming majority of the Shia, the people who are [lay], are Muslims: people who've been misguided. They've been told things that are not correct. They're not upon the correct tradition. So they're Muslims. So if they are Muslims, then I'm with the Muslim against the non-Muslim any day. So if my Muslim brothers and sisters are being attacked, the enemies attacking them, Zionism, the state of Israel, whatever name you want to give to them, then I'm against that 100%. There's no doubt about that.", "But at the same time, we got to separate between governments and people. That's where people get confused. You got to separate between scholars and layman. Scholars who know the truth, these people, scholars would say about these specific people, they're not Muslims, because they know the truth and they still call upon other than Allah. They still tell the people to do the wrong things and they misguide the lay people. So there's a difference between the lay people and the scholars.", "I don't necessarily need to support governments. I'm putting a blanket statement, including governments in the Middle East, government outside the Middle East. Muslim 