#passage(("This video is apparently \"What if the real sunnah is not what you thought?\" and talks about how to pray. And this is a very common phenomenon: you have people who are hired by certain individuals, and paid, and then they give them these studios, and they pay them this specific amount of money, and they make all of these dramatic effects and whatever to produce these videos, very carefully scripted videos. Probably hired by someone as a plant to pretend he's neither Sunni or Shi'a: \"Look, forget about sect guys, I'm objective!\" He's probably a Shi'a 100%. He's pretending he's not, and he's going to tell you some things, probably in his videos, that you would agree with, so he can pretend: I'm not Sunni or Shi'a, I'm an objective person.", "So he says: \"did the Prophetﷺ fold his hand when he was praying?\" Yes, the Prophet DID fold his hands when praying. Where do we get our habits from? We got them from Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him. Prophetﷺ told us صَلُّوا كما رَأَيْتُموني أُصلِّي (Pray as you've seen me praying). He also said: خُذُوا عَنِّي مَناسِكَكُم (take your traditions and religious practices from me). So we have multiple Ahadith, multiple Narrations that describe how to pray, and we took these. For example, alAlbani has a Book that says: صفةُ صلاةِ النّبي (The description of the prayer of the Prophetﷺ). And he brings all of these Narrations from the Companions, people who lived with the Prophet, seeing the Prophet and describing how the Prophet prayed. Did the Prophet fold his hand? Yes, he did in these Narrations, and that's why we fold our hands.", "So, \"let's look at history like a detective\"! \"Which chain is more authentic?\" It's just like he's making all of these preparations to make you think this guy's objective, and he's just doing historical analysis, but he's clearly following a view. He says \"everyone follows a view\". Exactly! You also follow a view. So don't pretend to us right now like you're just given this objective analysis.", "He says Sunni Muslims follow the 4 schools of thought and Shi'a follow Imam Jaafar asSadiq or the 12 Imams. But then he says, especially Jaafar asSadiq, because he knows that 90% or 95% of Narrations come only from two people, alBaqir and asSadiq, and mainly Jaafar asSadiq, from this liar Zurara. He knows that; that's why he has to say \"especially\", because it's not really from the 12 Imams. They don't learn how to pray from 'Ali. They don't learn how to pray from alHassan and alHussayn and the rest of the Imams.", "But then he says Muslims take the religion from the 4 Imams. That's a LIE. We don't take our religion ONLY from the 4 Imams. We don't trace our religion back to the 4 Imams. The 4 Imams, there are people who are earlier than them, that they took the religion from. Ahmad, ashShafi'i, alBukhari, all of these people, and then we go back now to who? We go back to التابعين (atTabi'in: the followers): Ibn Sirin, and all of these Tabi'in, and then we go back even earlier to the الصحابة (asSahaba: the Companions of the Prophetﷺ). This is who we actually take our religion from: from the Prophet, and the Companions around him who taught us how the Prophetﷺ prayed and what he did. So he starts with this red herring, pretending that we only take our religion from the 4 Imams, and then he wants to compare Ja'farasSadiq, specifically, with the 4 Imams. Well, that doesn't work! Because we don't take our religion from the 4 Imams. That's not where the chain stops. We take our religion directly from Prophet Muhammad.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Proves Jesus Is God?! Sunnis Don't Pray Like The Prophet?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qbnzQHBdTJo", ((931, "15:31–16:41"), (1013, "16:53–17:34"), (1070, "17:50–18:07"), (1101, "18:21–18:47"), (1132, "18:52–19:42"),))
// U ML108:572-671 | The Muslim Lantern | 7
#passage(("This guy, reading things, he doesn't know what he's talking about. He can't even know how to say the name of Abu Hanifa – \"Abu Hanafi\" he says.", "Where does the folding hand come from? It comes from tens of Narrations we have, where it explicitly says (Prophetﷺ put his right hand over his left hand). So we have this Narration saying the Prophetﷺ folded his hand: he put the right hand on top of the left hand. So we have these Narrations, tens of Narrations, from the Sahaba – from the Companions. This is where it comes from.", "Now, then, he says \"Imam Malik did that\". You're a liar! He didn't do that. That is a lie. Where is this report? Show me this report that says Imam Malik prayed with his hands down. That is a lie. And you said the people of Medina. That's another lie. There are no Narrations from the people of Medina praying with their hands down. There was a misunderstanding of one of the statements of Imam Malik, which is why, later, some people started to pray that way. Imam Malik was referring specifically to reclining on your hand, in a chapter which is talking about reclining on something while praying, if you're tired, and he was talking about كَراهَة (Karaha: abomination). But Imam Malik reports in the \"Muwatta\" the same Narration I'm telling you, about the Prophetﷺ placing his right hand over his left hand. So you are a liar, and there's nothing from Imam Malik that says that.", "And Ibn 'Abd alBarr himself, which is the pillar of the Maliki Madhab, anyone who follows the Maliki Madhab, he knows, he wrote these two: الاِستِذكار (alIstidhkar: The Recollection), and التَّمهيد (atTamheed: The Groundwork), the two main Books that explain the works of Imam Malik. And he says that the Sunnah, the right way to follow the Prophet Muhammadﷺ, and he's a Maliki, he says the right way is folding the hands, putting the right hand on the left hand. This is how the Prophetﷺ prayed. And he says that Imam Malik didn't oppose this view. And then we have many other scholars that we can go on and on, and mention, and explain.", "ashShafi'i is not on the chest; actually ashShafi'i is above the belly button.", "He says no consistency in \"folding\" reports. Look at the other fallacy he's committing here, the other strawman. He says inconsistency is about folding reports. These are not about folding. These reports are about the \"positioning\" of the hands. So if you already have the hands folded right over the left, where do you position them? So yeah, there's multiple reports about that, and all of them are accepted. We don't mind if you put it here, you put it there. It's not an issue; they're all accepted. The Prophetﷺ could have placed them in multiple places? Yes! Then your issue is fixed. But it's not about the folding. It's about the positioning of the hands.", "He says it's not a mass-transmission. I already told you there are tens of Companions reporting that the Prophetﷺ put his right hand over his left hand, and it's not isolated reports. So stop lying and saying \"let's think logically\" and \"being objective\".",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Proves Jesus Is God?! Sunnis Don't Pray Like The Prophet?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qbnzQHBdTJo", ((1665, "27:45–27:47"), (1674, "27:54–28:12"), (1694, "28:14–28:50"), (1734, "28:54–29:22"), (1771, "29:31–29:33"), (1787, "29:47–30:27"), (1833, "30:33–30:42"),))

