#passage(("Sunni and Shia is a political thing that happened after the Prophet. Prophetﷺ died, then we had the first Caliphate, Abu Bakr. He died, then the second Caliphate. He died, then the 3rd Caliph came; he was called 'Uthmanؓ. That third Caliphate: there was a group of rebellious people, who were not following Islam, not following the religion, who plotted to kill him, and they rioted around his house trying to kill him. He didn't fight them. In the end, they killed him.", "'Uthman was a relative of a person called Mu'awiya. They were both relatives. After 'Uthman, 'Ali took the leadership of the Muslims. Mu'awiya told 'Ali that I want to avenge the blood of 'Uthman from the people who killed him: I want justice; people killed my relative and I want justice to happen. But 'Ali had a different vision. 'Ali said that right now things are not stable; Muslims are also fighting the Roman and Persian Empires, they're trying to expand. Things were not stable, and these people, if we bring them to justice, other people will show up and there will be riots and problems. So there were two visions: one person had his right, he wanted to avenge the blood of his relative, and the other person saw things from a different perspective, that we need to wait. There was a disagreement happening. So Mu'awiya said: \"I'm not going to pledge allegiance to you\", \"I'm not going to choose you as my leader, until you avenge the blood of 'Uthman\". All of these now are political issues. All of these are issues that took place in the past, that are not related to the Scripture of Islam.", "So there were then two groups: a group aligned with Mu'awiya, that agreed with him that there should be that, and a group that was with 'Ali, that agreed we should wait. And there is a third group that stayed away from the whole thing. Both of them had armies, and they were trying to reconcile between one another. But this rebellious group that killed 'Uthman, they went and attacked one army, and they said \"The other army attacked you\". And they went to the other army and they did the same thing. And then war started between these two armies.", "Then later on, the group of people who aligned themselves with 'Ali called themselves Shia: شيعة علي (Shi'atu 'Ali: People who aligned themselves with 'Ali). The other Muslims, they say we follow the Prophetﷺ. That's what Sunnah means: to follow the Prophetﷺ. That's it! So we had a group of people coming because of political views; later on, they started developing beliefs. Like 'Ali died; they said \"No, 'Ali didn't die, he's going to come back\"; they started a creed called الرّجعَة (Raj'ah: coming back), that he's going to come back. He's a Human being! Why are you saying he's gonna come back? He died; everyone dies. Then they started a new Religion. They said \"OK, it's not only 'Ali. There are other 12 appointed Imams, and they know everything, and they don't make mistakes.\" All of that is not in the Quran! Political, that changed later on into people creating a Religion out of it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Iceland Visitors Enquire About Islam! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xigQO8G9dOo", ((891, "14:51–15:11"), (918, "15:18–16:14"), (980, "16:20–16:46"), (1011, "16:51–17:30"),))
