#passage(("It's all to do with history. It's not a theological thing. It became a theological thing later. It was never a theological thing in the beginning.", "There was a companion of the prophet, the third caliphate. He was assassinated. And then the fourth caliphate, who took the leadership after him, he saw that militant groups that killed that third caliphate are still there, and now it's not a good time, because we don't know exactly who did it. If we bring them all together, there will be [riots]. Then fighting happened. This is the battle of the [Jamal].", "Then later on, religious belief started to develop. Then started saying: no, actually he was supposed to be the first caliphate, but they took it away from him. No, he's actually infallible, and he knows the unseen, and he controls the universe; and then all the people who come from his lineage are all infallible people that are divinely appointed by Allah, like the pope: idea that came later on. I'm talking hundreds of years later. So if that comes later on, that's not a disagreement because of the interpretation of the Quran; it's not based on the Quran. It's based on a historical event.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Catholic Attempts To Disprove Islam Using Catholicism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lzIJWroR7Ec", ((3337, "55:37–55:46"), (3346, "55:46–57:09"), (3451, "57:31–58:17"),))
// U ML337:865-890 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Caliphate means a Leader. The Shias, they follow Ali, they [revere] Ali رضي الله عنه (may Allah be pleased with him), and we do as well, but they go in exaggeration. They say that we should follow him and all of his lineage etc.", "When Ali ibn abi Talib became the leader, Mu'awiya came to Ali and he said I want to avenge the blood of Uthman. So Ali رضي الله عنه said to him that we just sent an army to Rome and this and that; things are not stable; later on I will deal with this issue, but not right now. So he didn't say no. He said not now, it's not the time. And then a battle happened at this disagreement, and then things were solved later on.", "But the point is: all of the beliefs that I'm telling you about started to develop later on historically, because they're not in the Quran or in the Sunnah. If they were, we would have to believe them too.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Skeptical About The Prophet of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QIxWrKc_J_Y", ((2329, "38:49–39:13"), (2353, "39:13–39:43"), (2386, "39:46–39:58"),))
// U ML224:108-152 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("I don't identify myself as this, as that. I'll tell you why I identify myself as a Muslim: because the Quran that we're all supposed to follow says to call yourself a Muslim. The prophet, he said: name yourself Muslims, as Allah named you in the Quran. And Allah said: I named you Muslim. So if Allah names me Muslim, means follower, submitter, the one who submits to God. If my parents [name] me Muhammad, and I call myself Muhammad, if God the almighty names me something, I'm not going to go with people's names over it. I'm going to go with the God almighty's name over anyone else's naming me.", "Second thing, about the idea of [Sunni]: it's not like people imagine, 5050. Shia are like 10% of Muslims [or] less. Where's the difference coming from? [Shia] and [Sunnis] both believe in the same Quran, both believe in the same Prophet, both believe in the same God. But the difference comes from a historical event after the death of the Prophet. It's a political [succession]: a political thing that happened after the death of the Prophet: who should have been the successor, should have been Abu [Bakr] or should have been Ali. And then there was a new religion that was brought later on; they started bringing beliefs: oh, Ali is actually like God.", "I'm telling you history now. If you can find me, for example, at the time of the Prophet, anyone who said that Ali knew the Unseen or that Ali is going to come back to life: none of these things will be there. You'll find out that it happened later on, where these beliefs started to develop. So right now I'm speaking objectively that this is the case. Of course [a Shia] would say, no, no, that's not the case, but you can ask [him]: can you produce for me a [carbon-dated] manuscript of beliefs, where evidences that traces back that these people believe the things that you're saying? He's not going to be able to do that, and therefore that's objective history.", "Now what does Sunni mean? Sunni, it comes from the word which is tradition: to follow the tradition of the Prophet. If you go to [a Shia] and say to him, should we follow the tradition of the Prophet? You know what he's going to say? He's going to say yes. So by extension, in that way, just means to follow the tradition of the Prophet.", "Now in the end, call yourself potato, call yourself Sunni, call yourself [Shia]: the Quran is the criteria, because we all believe in it. And the Quran teaches that, for example, the companions of the Prophet, we should follow them; you'll have cursing them. We have the Quran, for example, saying that we should call upon Allah alone; you should worship Allah alone and call upon him alone; you find calling upon Ali and other dead people. So when you use the criteria, which is the Quran (Allah says, if you disagree over anything, return it to the Quran), if we use the Quran and we find the people doing anything, whether you call yourself Sunni, [Shia], potato, whatever you want to call yourself, if you're not doing what the Quran is saying and what the prophet taught, then you are wrong in that thing. The name is not going to save you, just by calling yourself something.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Man Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-rSkeAMTyK0", ((416, "6:56–7:27"), (447, "7:27–8:15"), (495, "8:15–8:47"), (527, "8:47–9:03"), (543, "9:03–9:46"),))
