ly mentions that the people in Sham and elsewhere during his time were making vows to graves, calling upon them, and were performing every act of worship they can for them, entailing glorification, submission, reverence, humility and dependence; and that during this time most Muslim mosques had a grave or something close to it; and that the silence is not an excuse for its validity. Now I don't think that Daniel actually believes that those things are Akbar, because Daniel actually excuses stuff that's way worse than this. Even Senusi, who came a couple of centuries earlier, said that many Bedawins denied that they would be resurrected in the afterlife. And for some reason, Daniel seems to believe that this is an argument against Muhammad.",), "Farid Responds, “My Reaction to Wahhabism Video + Debate Challenge”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zfe0bjwAAl4", ((97, "1:37–3:34"), (253, "4:13–5:22"), (421, "7:01–9:39"), (579, "9:39–10:27"), (681, "11:21–12:15"), (735, "12:15–14:23"),))

